---
import StarlightPage from '@astrojs/starlight/components/StarlightPage.astro';

// Every cell cites a source recorded in this repo; update the date and sources together.
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
const blob = 'https://github.com/lemun/kitzur/blob/main/';
const reviewed = 'October 23, 2026';
const sources = [
	{ n: 1, href: `${blob}DESIGN.md`, text: 'Kitzur design (DESIGN.md)' },
	{ n: 2, href: `${blob}README.md#benchmarks`, text: 'Kitzur README: what is kept, summarized and lost' },
	{ n: 3, href: `${blob}bench/opencode-sim.ts`, text: 'OpenCode compaction mechanics as read from OpenCode source and modelled offline (bench/opencode-sim.ts)' },
	{ n: 4, href: `${blob}CONFIG.md#client-setup-opencode-and-kilo`, text: 'Client setup: OpenCode and Kilo (CONFIG.md)' },
	{ n: 5, href: `${blob}bench/systems/gobstopper.ts`, text: 'How the benchmark launches gobstopper v0.7.2 (bench/systems/gobstopper.ts)' },
	{ n: 6, href: `${blob}THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md`, text: 'Third-party notices: what Kitzur adapted from gobstopper v0.7.2 (commit e894097)' },
	{ n: 7, href: `${blob}bench/README.md#historical-gobstopper-comparison`, text: 'Historical Gobstopper comparison (bench/README.md)' },
	{ n: 8, href: `${blob}docs/GOBSTOPPER-INTEROP.md`, text: 'Gobstopper legacy stats interop (docs/GOBSTOPPER-INTEROP.md)' },
];
---

<StarlightPage
	frontmatter={{
		title: 'Compare',
		description:
			'How Kitzur behaves next to an agent’s own compaction and Gobstopper, dimension by dimension, with sources.',
	}}
>
	<p>
		<strong>Reviewed {reviewed}.</strong> This compares behaviour, not quality. Each cell cites a
		source in the Kitzur repository. The native column describes OpenCode’s compaction as modelled in
		Kitzur’s benchmark. The Gobstopper column describes v0.7.2, the version Kitzur adapted code from and
		benchmarked. Later releases of either may behave differently. Kitzur was inspired by Gobstopper.
	</p>

	<table>
		<thead>
			<tr>
				<th>Dimension</th>
				<th>Kitzur</th>
				<th>Native client compaction (OpenCode)</th>
				<th>Gobstopper v0.7.2</th>
			</tr>
		</thead>
		<tbody>
			<tr>
				<th scope="row">Where it runs</th>
				<td>Loopback proxy between the agent and its model server <sup>[1]</sup></td>
				<td>Inside the agent <sup>[3]</sup></td>
				<td>Local proxy, a separate Rust binary <sup>[5]</sup></td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<th scope="row">Who writes the summary</th>
				<td>Deterministic extraction. No model is called <sup>[1]</sup></td>
				<td>The model, in a separate summarization request <sup>[3]</sup></td>
				<td>Mechanical: the head, summary and recent tail layout Kitzur adapted came via Gobstopper <sup>[6]</sup></td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<th scope="row">When it compacts</th>
				<td>When a request would exceed the prompt budget for the served window, below the client’s own compaction point <sup>[1]</sup></td>
				<td>When the last step’s prompt plus completion reaches the context minus min(output, 32,000), or after the provider reports an overflow <sup>[3][4]</sup></td>
				<td>At a configurable token threshold (<code>--threshold</code>) <sup>[5][7]</sup></td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<th scope="row">What stays word for word</th>
				<td>System prompts, tool definitions and recent messages, with tool calls kept next to their results <sup>[1][2]</sup></td>
				<td>The newest user turns, within 2,000 to 15,000 estimated tokens. The original goal is not kept verbatim <sup>[3]</sup></td>
				<td>A configurable recent tail (<code>--keep-recent</code>) <sup>[5][7]</sup></td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<th scope="row">Large tool output</th>
				<td>Old snapshots become stubs; other oversized results keep a head and tail <sup>[1]</sup></td>
				<td>Cut to 2,000 characters in the summarizer’s input <sup>[3]</sup></td>
				<td>Not covered by the sources here</td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<th scope="row">Repeated prefixes</th>
				<td>Forwarded messages stay unchanged between compactions under the default policy <sup>[1]</sup></td>
				<td>After compaction the model sees the system prompt, the summary, the tail and a continue message <sup>[3]</sup></td>
				<td>In-memory, content-addressed prefix store <sup>[5]</sup></td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<th scope="row">Wire formats</th>
				<td>OpenAI Chat Completions only <sup>[1]</sup></td>
				<td>Whatever the agent’s provider uses</td>
				<td>Separate OpenAI, Anthropic and ChatGPT upstreams <sup>[5]</sup></td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<th scope="row">Historical <code>qa46-ref</code> run, 100k/32k: planted facts</th>
				<td>7/7 (Kitzur predecessor, defaults) <sup>[7]</sup></td>
				<td>Not evaluated <sup>[7]</sup></td>
				<td>4/7 (tuned) <sup>[7]</sup></td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<th scope="row">Same run: prompt tokens, all attempts</th>
				<td>1,710,746 <sup>[7]</sup></td>
				<td>2,492,784 <sup>[7]</sup></td>
				<td>1,734,118 <sup>[7]</sup></td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<th scope="row">Stats</th>
				<td>JSONL stats that a Gobstopper release with <code>data import-legacy</code> can import as estimates <sup>[8]</sup></td>
				<td>Not covered by the sources here</td>
				<td>JSONL stats ledger <sup>[5]</sup></td>
			</tr>
		</tbody>
	</table>

	<h2 id="reading">Reading the table</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>
			Kitzur does not replace native compaction. Keep the agent’s own compaction on as a fallback;
			OpenCode’s automatic compaction is also how it recovers from an overflow <sup>[4]</sup>.
		</li>
		<li>
			The historical rows are simulated sessions against a mock server, measured before scenario
			sanitation. They are not a test of current Gobstopper or of real-model quality, and are not
			comparable with the <a href={`${base}/benchmarks/`}>current benchmark figures</a> <sup>[7]</sup>.
		</li>
		<li>Fact counts show whether planted markers survive, not whether a model understands them.</li>
	</ul>

	<h2 id="sources">Sources</h2>
	<ol>
		{sources.map((s) => <li id={`source-${s.n}`}><a href={s.href}>{s.text}</a></li>)}
	</ol>
</StarlightPage>
